• VERDICT: REQUEST_CHANGES

  **P0**: none

  **P1**:
  - `packages/hobo-ci/src/bitwarden-sign-in.ts:113-115` — `.catch()` handles asynchronous `requestCaptures` rejections but not a synchronous throw. That error escapes the outer handler unchanged, bypassing the explicit owner-channel refusal and potentially exposing raw channel error details. Wrap invocation with `Promise.resolve().then(...)`, as done for `approve` and `chooseOrganization`, and add a synchronous-throw regression test asserting a sanitized refusal without secret or channel-error text.

  **P2**:
  - `docs/ci/findings/0155-private-1password-owner-channels-built-not-proven.md:11-40` — both 1Password capture and reuse-attestation channels remain production-unobserved. Keep treating them as built-not-proven until the two referenced production runs are linked.

